==Trivia==
*The word ''rancour'', first appearing in Middle English, is defined as ''ire'', ''wrath'', and/or ''bitterness''. It can be traced back to Latin ''rancere'', meaning [https://www.etymonline.com/word/rancour "to stink"]. The word ''rancid'' shares this root.

